# P0095: unattended venus observation round 3 - early USB live log +
# hardware watchdog backstop.
#
# Design doc: docs/P0095_UNATTENDED_DESIGN.md (Q1-Q6 conclusions, risk
# table R1-R8, SOP). Rebased onto CI run 39328388718 (20c4cae, carries
# P0093+P0094), baseline tree ~/research/bt93 on the notebook.
#
# Phase A (boot-arg sweetusb=2, default off): bring the gadget + a
# raw-frame UDP console-ring pump up in kernel_bootstrap, BEFORE
# bsd_init - the observed venus death wall (mac_policy_initbsd+) sits
# before the existing mountroot probe, so rounds boot#22-25 died with
# zero bytes captured. DLIL/ifnet/sockets do not exist there, so the
# pump builds Ethernet/IPv4/UDP frames by hand and hands them straight
# to the EP_TX bulk endpoint; constants are the file's own (host MAC
# 02:00:5e:77:ee:01, phone ..:02, 192.168.7.1/2, UDP/5140 - mirrors
# tools/sweet-usbnet.sh). GCC clocks are echoed read-only only; venus's
# 0x088e2000 is the EUD manager and is never written. Everything fails
# soft - loss of the log never blocks bsd_init.
#
# Hardware WDT (default on, boot-arg sweetwdt=0 to disable): msm-watchdog
# map at 0x17c10000 per design Q3 ([VERIFIED], re-checked against
# MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource venus-r-oss qcom_soc_wdt.c: RST 0x04,
# EN 0x08, STS 0x0c, BARK 0x10, BITE 0x14, HZ 32765). BARK is programmed
# past BITE (XNU has no handler for the bark SPI0), BITE = 60 s; the
# watchdog is fed from (1) sweet_early_mark, (2) the bsd_init P0092
# mark sites, (3) a dedicated 15 s feed thread, (4) the sweet USB event
# + pump threads and (5) throttled from the console-ring append. A wedge
# stops being fed and the SoC bite-resets into recovery; the breed is
# readable from bootinfo.pureason bit0. The shim (vp4 line) arms it
# before the kernel jump and echoes the pre-arm EN/STS/BARK/BITE.
#
# All new code is #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) gated.
